course: dictionary
lesson: 10695
title: Unsafe and feeling unsafe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unsafe means dangerous: something that is likely to cause harm or injury. «The stairs were broken, so they were unsafe to climb.» Broken stairs could hurt you, so unsafe means not safe.
explain: You can also feel unsafe. That means you think you might be in danger. «It is okay to say no to any adult if what they ask makes you feel unsafe.» The feeling is a warning, and it matters.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in a word. «The ice was unsafe.» If you put in dangerous and the sentence still makes sense, you have got it. If someone makes you feel unsafe, stop, get away and tell a trusted adult.
fact: Unsafe means dangerous; likely to cause harm or injury.
fact: Feeling unsafe means feeling that you might be in danger.
fact: «Unsafe to drink» means the water may make you ill.
fact: Signs say «Danger: unsafe building» to warn people to keep away.
fact: If something feels unsafe, stop, get away and tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «The old bridge looked broken, so the sign said it was unsafe.» What does unsafe mean here? | Easy to cross | Very quiet | *Dangerous, likely to cause harm | Clean and shiny
exercise: Mia says, «The water is unsafe to drink.» What does this tell you? | The water is only for washing cars | The water is sweet and fresh | *The water may make you ill | The water is very cold
exercise: Which of these is an unsafe thing to do? | Washing your hands before lunch | *Playing with fire | Reading a book in bed | Drawing a picture
test: «Feeling unsafe means feeling that you might be in danger.» What does feeling unsafe mean? | Feeling proud of yourself | Feeling very tired | *Feeling that you might be in danger | Feeling bored
test: Jayden feels unsafe when an adult asks him to keep a secret. What should he do? | *Stop, get away and tell a trusted adult | Argue with the adult until they stop | Keep the secret forever | Ignore the feeling and say nothing
exam: Which word could replace unsafe in «The ice was unsafe»? | Cosy | Sunny | Warm | *Dangerous
